Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Disables Hardware-accelerated GPU Scheduling (HAGS), a Windows 10/11
; feature that can trigger early-launch crashes in BG3 on newer NVIDIA
; drivers. Import as administrator, then REBOOT. To re-enable: set HwSchMode
; to 1 (or delete the value) and reboot.
;
; The same operation via the Windows GUI:
;   Settings > System > Display > Graphics > "Change default graphics
;   settings" > turn off "Hardware-accelerated GPU scheduling" > reboot.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\GraphicsDrivers]
"HwSchMode"=dword:00000000
